<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Pym</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1584–1643</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Pym was an English parliamentarian who led the opposition to Charles I in the Short and Long Parliaments of 1640. He promoted the Grand Remonstrance of 1641 and was one of the Five Members whom the king tried to arrest in January 1642. A leading investor in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/providence-island-company">Providence Island Company</a>, he arranged Parliament's alliance with the Scots shortly before his death in 1643.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-pym.jpg" alt="John Pym" width="320" height="388" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edward Bower · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_Pym.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
